cq("c-arr-max-min", "Largest and Smallest", "EASY", T, "Print `Maximum: <x>` and `Minimum: <y>` on two lines.", "First line `n`, then `n` integers.", "Two lines.", SORTED,
   '    int mx = a[0], mn = a[0];\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n        if (a[i] > mx) mx = a[i];\n        if (a[i] < mn) mn = a[i];\n    }\n    printf("Maximum: %d\\nMinimum: %d\\n", mx, mn);', [arr([3, 9, 1]), arr([5]), arr([-4, -9, -1]), arr([100, 50, 75, 200]), arr([2, 2, 2])], A)
